Image fragments
description: a pixel rectangle on the image itself
- >
  An **image fragment** is a rectangle in the image's own **pixel coordinates**: `x`, `y` from the
  image's top-left corner, `w`, `h` the rectangle's size, all at the image's natural (unzoomed)
  resolution:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  type: rect
  x: 210
  y: 148
  w: 320
  h: 96
- >
  Zooming and panning in the viewer never change the stored numbers - they name pixels of the
  image, not of the screen. The fragment also embeds a PNG crop of the region ([the crop sidecar](*::annotations:fragments:crop)).
